## Visual Design & Branding

The heatmap visualization follows the agency’s official gradient system, transitioning from **orange → coral → pink → purple → periwinkle**.

### Brand Gradient Reference

Primary gradient progression:

- Orange → #F7A531  
- Coral → #FF7A4F  
- Pink → #F9485F  
- Magenta → #D85C8C  
- Purple → #9B7FD1  
- Periwinkle → #8C88D6  

This gradient reflects the agency’s visual identity and will be used consistently across heatmap visualizations.

---

## Heatmap Gradient Configuration

The heatmap uses a custom gradient aligned with the brand:

```js
const heatmap = h337.create({
  container: document.getElementById('heatmap-container'),
  gradient: {
    0.1: "#8C88D6",  // periwinkle (low)
    0.3: "#9B7FD1",  // purple
    0.5: "#D85C8C",  // magenta
    0.7: "#F9485F",  // pink/red
    0.9: "#FF7A4F",  // coral
    1.0: "#F7A531"   // orange (high intensity)
  }
});

